# Agent Execution Guardrails

## Contract-first
- Before any endpoint, SignalR method, Named Pipe message, or DB query: inspect `src/HorizonControl.Shared` and the master spec.
- If a DTO/contract is missing, add it in `HorizonControl.Shared` first, `dotnet build`, then implement producers/consumers.

## OS boundary
- `HorizonControl.Api` / `HorizonControl.Shared`: Linux-safe `net8.0` only — no Win32 P/Invoke, `System.Windows.*`, DirectoryServices, or DPAPI.
- Win32 / DPAPI only in `HorizonWatchdog.Service`, `.Tray`, `.Updater` (`net8.0-windows`).

## Iteration
- One cohesive vertical slice per turn (e.g. Shared DTO → migration → API → test). Verify build before expanding.
- No unsolicited refactors; minimal diffs.
- No stubs / `NotImplementedException` / mock data in production handlers, P/Invoke wrappers, or security middleware.

## Verification before concluding
- C#: `dotnet build` on affected project/solution; fix nullability (`CS86xx`) and fire-and-forget async (`CS4014`).
- Web: `npm run typecheck` (or `tsc --noEmit`) and `npm run build`.
- Deploy: `docker compose config` / `caddy validate` when those files change.

## Cross-cutting engineering
- Network calls: `CancellationToken` timeouts, exponential backoff with jitter, offline/fallback behavior.
- Logging: `ILogger<T>` structured templates only — never `Console.WriteLine` in production services.
